  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through next Monday)\nIssued at 942 AM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nDry conditions persist through most of the day on Wednesday, but \nwe'll be watching an upper-level low and a cold front approach from \nthe west by that evening. Moisture advection ahead of the cold front \nwill bring a high chance for rain showers mainly Wednesday night \nbefore the front clears the area Thursday morning. Rain is still \nvery much needed, but this system doesn't look to bring much \nappreciable rain with forecast totals less than 0.25 inches. \nAdditional disturbances will keep low rain chances across the \nPlateau through Friday. The bigger impact with this system will be \nthe drop in temperatures. Thursday highs will only be in the 50s, \naround 10-15 degrees cooler compared to Wednesday. Friday will be \neven cooler with highs in the 40s areawide. A widespread freeze \nis then expected Friday night into Saturday morning with lows in \nthe mid to upper 20s. This will likely be Nashville's first \nfreeze of the season which will be a little later than the average\nfirst freeze of November 1st. Temperatures will slowly recover \nover the weekend and into next week with dry conditions \nprevailing.",
